review:
If anyone is familiar with [b]Alien Shooter[/b] title will get into really fast. The game focus in a simple shooter'em up genre which can be played not only on singleplayer which have fantastic gameplay or on cooperative mode. The story isn't important, the game bit by bit remember game themes like [b]Natural Selection[/b] combined with [b]DOOM[/b] and [b]Alien Swarm[/b], the controls aren't clanky like some pointed out to be is just point and shoot. 
But why is this similar to [b]Alien Shooter[/b]? Waves of nasty enemies coming at you...is tough so it is fun!

The perfomance on any 4-5 years old machine can handle this without struggle, tested on: [b]Intel® Core™2 Quad Q8300 2.50 GHz + NVIDIA - GeForce® GTX 750 Ti 2 GB + 8gb DDR2 RAM[/b], the fps won't drop beyond 38 frames which results the best and smooth experience ever.   

[u]The minor issues are:[/u]
[code][list]
    [*]Checkpoint in the campaign are really unfair, sometimes you are 60% to finish the level and upon death the checkpoint is reloaded to a small percenteage of the progress you had which is always at the beginning;
    [*]Also, you can't leave missions otherwise it will erase any progress you did forcing you to start all over again that level but don't be alarmed because one mission would take you an hour or less depending of your lack of skills;
    [*]Multiplayer don't need to be entirely cruel, you can play alone with bots and with assets from singleplayer;
[/list][/code]

So be prepared, be on company of your friends because you will spend hours and hours fighting hordes of demonic monsters in attempt to survive this apocalyptic world.
